# Cloudflare Pages redirect rules — canonical URL consolidation
#
# All canonical URLs are clean, slashless paths (except root `/`).
# Direct requests to `.html` alias files are permanently redirected (301)
# to their canonical slashless route so search engines consolidate signals
# onto a single URL per page.
#
# Note: Cloudflare Pages `_redirects` only supports redirect/rewrite status
# codes (200, 301, 302, 303, 307, 308). Do NOT add `404` status rules here —
# Cloudflare Pages rejects invalid status codes in `_redirects` and natively
# serves `/404.html` with HTTP status 404 for any unmatched path.

